# Testing — Definition of Done

For every non-trivial change to a `.ts` or `.tsx` file under `obra/src/`:

1. **Add or update** a colocated `*.test.ts` / `*.test.tsx` file that covers the changed behaviour.
2. **Run `npm run test`** in `obra/` before marking work as done. All tests must pass.
3. **No `|| true`** or `--passWithNoTests` in CI commands.

## What counts as "non-trivial"

| Counts | Exceptions (tests not required) |
|---|---|
| New pure function or utility | Pure type files (`*.d.ts`, type-only exports) |
| New React component with logic | Generated code or vendor output |
| Bug fix in existing logic | Index re-export files (`index.ts` with no logic) |
| New hook | Trivial one-liners with no branching |
| Auth / payments / credits change | Configuration files |

## Layer guidance

- **Unit:** mock all I/O at the module boundary (`vi.mock`). Prefer colocated mocks over `__mocks__/`.
- **Integration:** use MSW to intercept Supabase REST / Edge calls. Never use real Supabase credentials.
- **E2E:** backlog (Playwright) — not required for Sprint 1.

